{"id": 17, "ts": 1780658431.2087283, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I concur with Sarah\u2019s shift to Candidate\u202fC as the provisional choice. The 100\u202f% reliability record and the positive crew atmosphere reported for C directly address the operational reliability and crew\u2011cooperation criteria that are paramount for long\u2011haul flights. Moreover, C\u2019s ability to stay calm in a crisis and to make correct decisions quickly strengthens the stress\u2011resilience and decision\u2011quality dimensions.\nThe concerns you raised\u2014difficulty communicating ideas, an egocentric attitude, and limited willingness to pursue further education\u2014are real, but they appear less likely to jeopardize safety than the documented \u201cnasty remarks\u201d from Candidate\u202fB, which threaten crew cohesion, or the arrogance and hot temper noted for Candidate\u202fD, which could impair teamwork under pressure. Until we have evidence that C\u2019s communication style materially undermines cockpit coordination, his overall profile remains the strongest.\nI would still like clarification on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s decision\u2011quality and attention to detail, and any additional observations on Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation, to ensure we have a complete comparison, but based on the current evidence my vote stays with Candidate\u202fC."}
